    "region_label": "Prince William Forest",
    "description": "Prince William Forest Park — the largest protected natural area in the Washington, D.C. metro (~15,000 acres of Quantico Creek piedmont forest) near Triangle and Dumfries, Virginia. An NPS unit roughly bounded by Route 619 (south/west), Route 234 (north) and Interstate 95 (east), with ~37 miles of hiking trails and old CCC cabin camps. This region ships the park's REAL NPS boundary polygon, so the Phase-2 spatial curation is active: OSM ways whose representative point falls outside the park (I-95 frontage, Triangle/Dumfries streets, private inholdings) are soft-demoted, never dropped.",
